  "about": "Tool protocol the CLI's code may spell: the commands, flags and words of the tools it calls, and text mechanics. Every other literal is a value and lives in data (principle 11, docs/design/values.md). `numbers` are arithmetic (an index, a step, a pair, milliseconds per second, per hour and per day); any other number is a threshold or a size and lives in data. `host` is the coding agent's hook protocol, `cli` the CLI's own command and flag names, `mermaid` the diagram syntax, `github` the workflow keys it reads, `githubApi` the REST and GraphQL paths, flags and field types of the API the board calls, `openapi` the OpenAPI and JSON Schema words the contract checks read.",
